WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.230
Choose your platforms, and grow a real audience.

2
00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:08.060
This is the video for module one of Social Media Marketing for Business.

3
00:00:09.310 --> 00:00:18.380
Social media marketing helps the right people find your business, trust it and buy from it. It starts with knowing exactly who your customer is.

4
00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:23.940
A small business cannot do every platform well, so the skill is choosing.

5
00:00:25.190 --> 00:00:30.180
A stranger decides in a few seconds whether your profile looks real and trustworthy.

6
00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:35.310
And you will learn to grow an audience that buys, without paying for it.

7
00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:46.140
Step one. Write one sentence about your best customer: who she is, where she lives, what she needs, and how she likes to buy. This is your target audience.

8
00:00:47.390 --> 00:01:03.050
Step two. Pick one main platform where your customers discover businesses. Instagram suits anything visual, like fashion, beauty and food. TikTok suits products you can demonstrate. Facebook suits local services and community selling.

9
00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:09.120
Step three. Add one support platform where you share the best of the same content.

10
00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:22.000
Step four. Facebook, Instagram and TikTok help people discover you, but WhatsApp is where most Nigerian small businesses close the sale. So send every enquiry there.

11
00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:27.850
Step five. After 30 days, review using real enquiries, not likes.

12
00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:37.510
Funmi, who sells small chops in Ibadan, chose Facebook as main and Instagram as support, and gets every order in one WhatsApp inbox.

13
00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:45.390
Your profile must answer four questions fast. What do you sell? Where? Can I trust you? How do I order?

14
00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:55.210
Ada sells Ankara dresses in Abuja. Her old bio said, God's own designer, blessed, DM for enquiries. It answered none of them.

15
00:01:56.460 --> 00:02:07.700
She switched to a Business account and rewrote it: ready-to-wear Ankara dresses for work and owambe, sizes 8 to 20, delivery across Abuja, order on WhatsApp below.

16
00:02:08.050 --> 00:02:17.080
She added her wa.me link and Highlights for price list, reviews and how to order. Now a visitor can order without asking a single question.

17
00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:28.120
An algorithm is the set of rules an app uses to decide who sees each post. It predicts what each person will watch, comment on, save or share.

18
00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:36.240
Halima sells zobo in Kaduna. Her flyer with prices reached about 120 accounts, with only 2 saves.

19
00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:46.570
Her carousel, five ways to serve zobo at a party, reached about 400 accounts and was saved 35 times, because it was useful.

20
00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:55.400
Her short Reel of chilled zobo poured over ice reached about 1,900 accounts, mostly non-followers.

21
00:02:55.750 --> 00:03:04.340
So she now posts one useful carousel and two Reels a week, and keeps prices in a pinned post. Her own Insights beat any general rule.

22
00:03:05.590 --> 00:03:13.590
A content pillar is a theme you return to again and again. Most small businesses need three to five. Teach gives useful tips.

23
00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:19.320
Show the work proves your skill, like fabric to finished gown in 20 seconds.

24
00:03:20.570 --> 00:03:25.050
Proof builds trust with real customer reviews, always shared with permission.

25
00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:29.460
Behind the scenes shows the person behind the brand.

26
00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:37.650
And Offer asks for the sale clearly. Keep offers the smallest share, because people ignore a wall of adverts.

27
00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:43.330
Before posting, spend 5 minutes replying to comments on your last post.

28
00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:50.560
After posting, stay for 10 minutes. Early conversation is a positive signal to the app.

29
00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:56.860
Leave thoughtful comments on 5 posts from local customers, partners or groups.

30
00:03:58.110 --> 00:04:02.290
Share the new post to your WhatsApp Status, so existing contacts see it.

31
00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:14.700
And use a few specific keywords and hashtags, like Ankara dresses Abuja, instead of 30 general ones. Done three times a week, this takes about 30 minutes each time.

32
00:04:15.950 --> 00:04:28.580
Turn on two-factor authentication everywhere. Takeovers of Nigerian business pages often start with a fake support message, so never share a login code, even for a verified badge.

33
00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:39.870
Never buy followers. They do not buy from you, and they can reduce your reach. And always ask before posting a customer's photo, name or chat, with phone numbers blurred.

34
00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:57.590
To remember. Write your customer sentence first. Use one main platform, one support, and WhatsApp to close. Your bio says what, where, proof and how to order. Useful posts get saved and short Reels travel. And track enquiries, not just followers.

35
00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:07.570
Now choose your platforms, rewrite your bio with your wa.me link, audit your last nine posts, and plan 12 post ideas for your first month.

36
00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:10.070
Then continue with the lessons below.
